# Line endings.
#
# Prettier is configured `endOfLine: "lf"`, and CI runs `format:check` on a
# Linux checkout, where that is what it gets. On Windows, git's core.autocrlf
# writes CRLF into the working tree instead — so the same file that passes in
# CI fails locally, and `npm run format:check` reports dozens of files that
# git itself considers unmodified. The check becomes noise, and a developer
# learns to ignore it.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` settles it: git still normalises to LF in the object
# store, and now also checks out LF on every platform, so the working tree
# matches what CI and Prettier both expect.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted — doing so corrupts them.
# The brand artwork in particular is opaque PNG whose bytes matter: the app's
# bar colour is sampled to match the crop's own ground.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.mp4 binary
